# Every text file is committed and checked out with LF, whatever a clone's
# core.autocrlf says. The editor-ui suite pins source text with "\n", so a
# CRLF checkout (Git for Windows' default core.autocrlf=true) failed ten of
# its suites on this repo alone — the apps that vendor it as a submodule
# had each to document a per-clone config to undo that. Binary files are
# detected by content (text=auto) and left alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.wav binary
*.tile binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
